.\" Contact melchiorrecaruso@gmail.com to correct errors or typos.
.TH man 1 "22 NOV 2026" "0.5" "GULP man page"
.SH NAME
.B gulp
\- A simple journaling archiver.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR gulp " [-] s --synch | r --restore | p --purge | l --list | c --check | f --fix | h --help"
.RI " [ " options " ...] [ " files " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gulp
stores and extracts files from a disk archive. A GULP archive is a sequence of timestamped updates, each listing the files and directories that have been added, changed, or deleted since the previous transacted update.

The first argument to gulp should be a function; either one of the letters
.BR srplcfh ", or one of the long function names. A function letter needs to be prefixed with '-', and can't be combined with other single-letter options. A long function name must be prefixed with --.  Some options take a parameter; with the single-letter form these must be given as separate arguments. With the long form, they must be given by appending =value to the option."

.SH FUNCTION LETTERS
Main operation mode:

.BR \-s ", " --synch
.RS
append changes in
.IR files " to archive, or create archive if it does not exist. " files " is a list of file and directory names separated by spaces. If a name is a directory, then it recursively includes all files and subdirectories within. " files " may contain wildcards * and ? in the last component of the path (after the last slash). * matches any string and ? matches any character."

.RI "A change is an addition, update, or deletion of any file or directory in " files " or any of its subdirectories to any depth. A file or directory is considered changed if its type, size, last-modified date, Unix/Linux permissions or Windows attributes, or symbolic link target differ between the internal and external versions. File contents are not compared. Only files and directories within " files " are marked as deleted when they no longer exist."

.RI  "For each added or updated file or directory, the following information is saved in the archive: the contents, the file or directory name as it appears in " files " plus any trailing path, the last-modified date (UTC), and the Unix/Linux permissions or Windows attributes. Other metadata such as owner, group, last access time, etc. are not saved. Symbolic links are saved. Hard links are followed as if they were ordinary files. Special file types such as devices, named pipes, and named sockets are not saved. If any file cannot be read (e.g. permission denied), then it is skipped with a warning and retried at the next synch. However, other files are still added and the update is still valid. The archive itself is never added."

Updates are transacted. If an update fails, it is removed from the archive. If gulp is interrupted before completing the update, then the archive can be repaired with the fix function.
.RE

.BR \-r ", " --restore
.RS
.RI "restore " files " (including the contents of directories), or extract the whole archive contents if " files " is omitted. The file names, last-modified date, and permissions or attributes are set as saved in the archive. If there are multiple versions of a file stored, then only the latest version is extracted. If a stored file has been marked as deleted, then it is deleted. Existing files are overwritten if they are considered changed; a file is replaced only after its data has been verified."

.RI "Unless --nodelete is given, external files and directories within " files " that do not exist in the archive are deleted. Excluded items and the archive itself are never deleted."
.RE

.BR \-p ", " --purge
.RS
purge archive, remove old files archived. The archive is replaced only when the purged copy has been completely written.
.RE

.BR \-l ", " --list
.RS
.RI "list " files " within the archive, or list the entire archive contents if " files " is omitted. For each file or directory, show version number, marker, Unix/Linux permissions, attributes, last-modified date, size and name. Permissions are listed as an octal number (as per chmod(1)) and attributes with the letters R, H, S, V, D, A, L (read-only, hidden, system, volume, directory, archive, symbolic link)."
.RE

.BR \-c ", " --check
.RS
check archive integrity by verifying that the data agrees with the stored SHA-1 hashes and sizes and that the data otherwise conforms to the gulp standard.
.RE

.BR \-f ", " --fix
.RS
truncates any data added after last valid update.
.RE

.BR \-h ", " --help
.RS
show the help.
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
Operation modifiers:

.BR \-e ", " --exclude=\fIpattern\fR
.RS
exclude files in pattern. Can be repeated.
.RE

.BR \--excludeattr=\fIattributes\fR
.RS
exclude files with any of the attributes, given with the letters R, H, S, V, D, A, L.
.RE

.BR \--excludemode=\fImode\fR
.RS
exclude files with any of the permission bits in mode, given as an octal number.
.RE

.BR \--forcepath
.RS
allow files with absolute path names.
.RE

.BR \-i ", " --include=\fIpattern\fR
.RS
include files in pattern. Can be repeated.
.RE

.BR \--nodelete
.RS
with synch, do not mark files in the archive as deleted when the corresponding external file does not exist. With restore, do not delete external files when the corresponding file in archive does not exist. This makes gulp consistent with the behavior of most non-journaling archivers.
.RE

.BR \--only=\fIversion\fR
.RS
with list, show only the changes made in version.

.RS
gulp -l backup --only=20
.RE

show files added or deleted in version 20.
.RE

.BR \-u ", " --until=\fIversion\fR
.RS
ignore any part of the archive updated after version number.

.RS
gulp -l backup --until=20
.RE

show files added before version 21.
.RE

.BR \--verbose
.RS
show each processed file.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
Create archive.gulp from files foo and bar.

.RS
gulp -s archive.gulp foo bar

.RE
List all files in archive.gulp.

.RS
gulp -l archive.gulp

.RE
Restore all files from archive.gulp.

.RS
gulp -r archive.gulp

.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 if successful or 1 in case of an error.
.SH BUGS
The archive format does not save sufficient information for backing up and restoring the operating system.
